{"title":"2014 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> be a natural number. Show that the sum of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/9/9f95e9fc37dc276d9cfc43aba335cde356371cac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^{th}$\" width=\"22\" height=\"15\" /> powers of the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> positive\nintegers is a polynomial of degree <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/8/e18453e31b8b9f4f7722777b72a0eff030a17d1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" />, i.e.,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/7/dd7849a099d8a9f3c18139d930da73d6cd3715c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1^k + 2^k + 3^k + \\cdots + n^k = p_{k+1}(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"263\" height=\"20\" />,\nwhere <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/3/e1391390f33773f0a3a70d50b5e7958a7ad2d611.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_{k+1}(t)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" /> is a polynomial of degree <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/8/e18453e31b8b9f4f7722777b72a0eff030a17d1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" />. For example, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/f/00fab47c0b9d0ce398d03e57d6720129d53434f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> we have\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/2/352142a90b1e4d273301f3a0a4140ba18533c941.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1 + 2 +\\cdots + n = \\sum_{j=1}^{n} {j} = \\frac{n(n+1)}{2}=\\tfrac{1}{2}n^2+\\tfrac{1}{2}n\\]\" width=\"369\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/3/293d30cdd8866ae68ecbe843c07d314b8889d79b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_2(t) = \\tfrac{1}{2} t^2 + \\tfrac{1}{2}t.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"130\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By Faulhaber's Formula,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/8/3d84be5e1b7f3e86078630260808e8ca3fbdfb26.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1^k+2^k+\\cdots+n^k=\\frac{1}{k+1}\\sum_{i=0}^k {k+1\\choose i}b_i n^{k+1-i}\\]\" width=\"374\" height=\"53\" />\nwhere the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/d/94d9565abaadf04609a2e9941aa2d20b0a299b8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"15\" /> are given constants beyond the scope of this proof (the Bernoulli rationals). Clearly, considering the case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/6/3468ccd41bc761dcc455140089e3224a4b1b95e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i=0$\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" /> gives a term containing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/e/70ed95241a64932411fe17e761a07cc3644975e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^{k+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"17\" /> (note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/b/0fb213db54916ee753d8d1ea3b4c3237e6545d4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_0=1\\ne0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" />), and all smaller terms contain powers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> with exponent less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/5/f05f085f774fc8ab50676b778b86a1f1d1114fc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />; therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/3/e1391390f33773f0a3a70d50b5e7958a7ad2d611.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_{k+1}(t)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" /> is indeed a polynomial of degree <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/5/f05f085f774fc8ab50676b778b86a1f1d1114fc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />, and we are done.\n</p><p>~ <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Eevee9406\">eevee9406</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II\" title=\"2014 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II\">2014 UNM-PNM Contest II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems\" title=\"2014 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2014 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://mathcontest.unm.edu/\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2014 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2014 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2014 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2014 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2014 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_